  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 224 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nHigh pressure on Saturday will be more amplified with flow even more \nout of the south, that will really isolated the thunderstorm chances \nto just the west, unless the center of the high can move further \neast.  Still a medium chance of showers and storms for the western \nPanhandles and as a result those storms will probably just have \ngusty winds and heavy rain.  Sunday through Wednesday looks to be on \nthe dry side as the ridge is more pronounced over the area and the \nmoisture feed that we had been receiving is pushed west into NM.  \nStill will not rule out something clipping our area, if the models \nhave the ridge too far west.  Overall temperatures will still be \nrunning on the hot side, but currently it looks like we'll hold \nbelow heat advisory levels.  That being said, the heat impacts could \nstill be on the major side, just given that it's September and the \nhighs would usually be in the upper 80s and we haven't really had a \nbreak in these hot temperatures in a very long while.  \n\nWeber",
